{"3758950":{"success":true,"data":{"type":"game","name":"Death at Fleming Manor","steam_appid":3758950,"required_age":0,"is_free":false,"detailed_description":"<ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Over 120,000 wishlists before launch!<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Taipei Game Show 2027 – Best Design Finalist<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><\/li><\/ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Media Reviews<\/strong><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>&quot;Death at Fleming Manor is overwhelmingly a love letter to some of the OG detective writers.&quot;<\/i> <strong>— Grace Dean, The Wand Report (8\/10)<\/strong><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>&quot;An excellent indie game that beautifully succeeds in its unique approach of blending forensics with a thriller mystery adventure.&quot;<\/i> <strong>— 쿠타르크, This Is Game (8.4\/10)<\/strong><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>&quot;Experience the satisfying feeling of being outwitted, just like in a classic mystery novel.&quot;<\/i> <strong>— 本丸猫左衛門, 4Gamer<\/strong><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>&quot;Murderously Good. Between the clever deductions, varied investigations and unexpected twists, Death at Fleming Manor had me hooked.&quot;<\/i> <strong>— Sonia Heng, QuestDaily (9\/10)<\/strong><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>&quot;A unique art style and smart ideas that expand on the concept of playing as a coroner.&quot;<\/i> <strong>— James Gregory, Play Save Repeat (8\/10)<\/strong><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><i><strong>If you unraveled Return of the Obra Dinn and The Case of the Golden Idol to the very end...<\/strong><\/i><\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>It is time to pick up your pen.<\/strong><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Your job is to write the death certificate.<\/strong><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/3758950\/extras\/fcd0ccf0a7f931723b9ad705a383481b.poster.avif?t=1793692815\" width=800 height=486 ><source src=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/3758950\/extras\/fcd0ccf0a7f931723b9ad705a383481b.webm?t=1793692815\" type=\"video\/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/3758950\/extras\/fcd0ccf0a7f931723b9ad705a383481b.mp4?t=1793692815\" type=\"video\/mp4\"><\/video><\/span><\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>England, 1959<\/strong><\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A series of unexplained deaths has occurred at Fleming Manor, a country estate outside London.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >As the investigator assigned to the cases, you will examine each scene, study the condition of the body, question the people involved, and review the available evidence. You must identify the victim, determine the cause of death, and decide whether the death was accidental, self-inflicted, or the result of murder.<i> <\/i><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/3758950\/extras\/399fb4961bfa9498c8dd4c13f6ac1334.poster.avif?t=1793692815\" width=800 height=468 ><source src=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/3758950\/extras\/399fb4961bfa9498c8dd4c13f6ac1334.webm?t=1793692815\" type=\"video\/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/3758950\/extras\/399fb4961bfa9498c8dd4c13f6ac1334.mp4?t=1793692815\" type=\"video\/mp4\"><\/video><\/span><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >When you believe you understand what happened, record your conclusions in a death certificate or emergency report. Choosing a suspect is not enough. Missing or incorrect information may lead to the wrong conclusion.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/3758950\/extras\/6ce84e4ccda4fb031c18dcd50dd80d4d.poster.avif?t=1793692815\" width=800 height=468 ><source src=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/3758950\/extras\/6ce84e4ccda4fb031c18dcd50dd80d4d.webm?t=1793692815\" type=\"video\/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/3758950\/extras\/6ce84e4ccda4fb031c18dcd50dd80d4d.mp4?t=1793692815\" type=\"video\/mp4\"><\/video><\/span><\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Investigation at Fleming Manor<\/strong><\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Death at Fleming Manor<\/i> is a forensic mystery adventure built around observation, deduction, and official documentation.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game takes place in a British country manor in the late 1950s. Its hand-drawn visual style is inspired by European crime and mystery comics of the 1960s.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If you enjoy <strong>Agatha Christie<\/strong> mysteries, methodical investigations, and story-driven games where small details matter, <strong>Death at Fleming Manor<\/strong> may be for you.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/3758950\/extras\/02222c86d708e28003c972a23f79a41f.poster.avif?t=1793692815\" width=800 height=468 ><source src=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/3758950\/extras\/02222c86d708e28003c972a23f79a41f.webm?t=1793692815\" type=\"video\/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/3758950\/extras\/02222c86d708e28003c972a23f79a41f.mp4?t=1793692815\" type=\"video\/mp4\"><\/video><\/span><\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong><i>Key Features<\/i><\/strong><\/h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Complete the Official Records<\/strong> <br>Examine each body, review the evidence, and record your conclusions in death certificates and emergency reports.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>A Mystery Set in a 1950s British Manor<\/strong> <br>Investigate a series of deaths at an isolated country estate, where the residents may not be telling you everything.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Hand-Drawn Ligne Claire Artwork<\/strong> <br>Explore scenes illustrated by hand in a style inspired by European mystery comics from the 1960s.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Draw Your Own Conclusions<\/strong> <br>The game will not confirm your suspicions for you. To close a case, you must identify what happened and support every part of your report with evidence.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><br><strong>Video Upload &amp; Livestreaming Guidelines<\/strong><\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Monetization is permitted, including advertising revenue through platforms such as YouTube and Twitch. No prior permission is required. However, to prevent story spoilers, please follow the guidelines below:<\/p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Until November 10 (Tuesday) at 8:00 AM UTC (5:00 PM KST\/JST), <\/strong>please do not show the final episode (Episode 12) or any of the endings in videos or livestreams.<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>After November 10 at 8:00 AM UTC,<\/strong> you may show all episodes and endings.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><u><i><strong>Even after this date, please avoid including major story spoilers in video titles or thumbnails, where they could easily be seen by people who have not yet played the game.<\/strong><\/i><\/u><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Thank you for your understanding and cooperation.<br><br><br><br>All graphics in this game were created by human artists. No generative AI was used.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >We also have a YouTube channel where we upload introduction videos for our layered Clip Studio Paint files, as well as detailed videos showing the work process.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >YouTube: @SUPERTHUMbGameArt<\/p>","about_the_game":"<ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Over 120,000 wishlists before launch!<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Taipei Game Show 2027 – Best Design Finalist<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><\/li><\/ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Media Reviews<\/strong><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>&quot;Death at Fleming Manor is overwhelmingly a love letter to some of the OG detective writers.&quot;<\/i> <strong>— Grace Dean, The Wand Report (8\/10)<\/strong><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>&quot;An excellent indie game that beautifully succeeds in its unique approach of blending forensics with a thriller mystery adventure.&quot;<\/i> <strong>— 쿠타르크, This Is Game (8.4\/10)<\/strong><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>&quot;Experience the satisfying feeling of being outwitted, just like in a classic mystery novel.&quot;<\/i> <strong>— 本丸猫左衛門, 4Gamer<\/strong><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>&quot;Murderously Good. Between the clever deductions, varied investigations and unexpected twists, Death at Fleming Manor had me hooked.&quot;<\/i> <strong>— Sonia Heng, QuestDaily (9\/10)<\/strong><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>&quot;A unique art style and smart ideas that expand on the concept of playing as a coroner.&quot;<\/i> <strong>— James Gregory, Play Save Repeat (8\/10)<\/strong><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><i><strong>If you unraveled Return of the Obra Dinn and The Case of the Golden Idol to the very end...<\/strong><\/i><\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>It is time to pick up your pen.<\/strong><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Your job is to write the death certificate.<\/strong><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/3758950\/extras\/fcd0ccf0a7f931723b9ad705a383481b.poster.avif?t=1793692815\" width=800 height=486 ><source src=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/3758950\/extras\/fcd0ccf0a7f931723b9ad705a383481b.webm?t=1793692815\" type=\"video\/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/3758950\/extras\/fcd0ccf0a7f931723b9ad705a383481b.mp4?t=1793692815\" type=\"video\/mp4\"><\/video><\/span><\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>England, 1959<\/strong><\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A series of unexplained deaths has occurred at Fleming Manor, a country estate outside London.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >As the investigator assigned to the cases, you will examine each scene, study the condition of the body, question the people involved, and review the available evidence. You must identify the victim, determine the cause of death, and decide whether the death was accidental, self-inflicted, or the result of murder.<i> <\/i><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/3758950\/extras\/399fb4961bfa9498c8dd4c13f6ac1334.poster.avif?t=1793692815\" width=800 height=468 ><source src=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/3758950\/extras\/399fb4961bfa9498c8dd4c13f6ac1334.webm?t=1793692815\" type=\"video\/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/3758950\/extras\/399fb4961bfa9498c8dd4c13f6ac1334.mp4?t=1793692815\" type=\"video\/mp4\"><\/video><\/span><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >When you believe you understand what happened, record your conclusions in a death certificate or emergency report. Choosing a suspect is not enough. Missing or incorrect information may lead to the wrong conclusion.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/3758950\/extras\/6ce84e4ccda4fb031c18dcd50dd80d4d.poster.avif?t=1793692815\" width=800 height=468 ><source src=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/3758950\/extras\/6ce84e4ccda4fb031c18dcd50dd80d4d.webm?t=1793692815\" type=\"video\/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/3758950\/extras\/6ce84e4ccda4fb031c18dcd50dd80d4d.mp4?t=1793692815\" type=\"video\/mp4\"><\/video><\/span><\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Investigation at Fleming Manor<\/strong><\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Death at Fleming Manor<\/i> is a forensic mystery adventure built around observation, deduction, and official documentation.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game takes place in a British country manor in the late 1950s. Its hand-drawn visual style is inspired by European crime and mystery comics of the 1960s.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If you enjoy <strong>Agatha Christie<\/strong> mysteries, methodical investigations, and story-driven games where small details matter, <strong>Death at Fleming Manor<\/strong> may be for you.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/3758950\/extras\/02222c86d708e28003c972a23f79a41f.poster.avif?t=1793692815\" width=800 height=468 ><source src=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/3758950\/extras\/02222c86d708e28003c972a23f79a41f.webm?t=1793692815\" type=\"video\/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/3758950\/extras\/02222c86d708e28003c972a23f79a41f.mp4?t=1793692815\" type=\"video\/mp4\"><\/video><\/span><\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong><i>Key Features<\/i><\/strong><\/h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Complete the Official Records<\/strong> <br>Examine each body, review the evidence, and record your conclusions in death certificates and emergency reports.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>A Mystery Set in a 1950s British Manor<\/strong> <br>Investigate a series of deaths at an isolated country estate, where the residents may not be telling you everything.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Hand-Drawn Ligne Claire Artwork<\/strong> <br>Explore scenes illustrated by hand in a style inspired by European mystery comics from the 1960s.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Draw Your Own Conclusions<\/strong> <br>The game will not confirm your suspicions for you. To close a case, you must identify what happened and support every part of your report with evidence.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><br><strong>Video Upload &amp; Livestreaming Guidelines<\/strong><\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Monetization is permitted, including advertising revenue through platforms such as YouTube and Twitch. No prior permission is required. However, to prevent story spoilers, please follow the guidelines below:<\/p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Until November 10 (Tuesday) at 8:00 AM UTC (5:00 PM KST\/JST), <\/strong>please do not show the final episode (Episode 12) or any of the endings in videos or livestreams.<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>After November 10 at 8:00 AM UTC,<\/strong> you may show all episodes and endings.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><u><i><strong>Even after this date, please avoid including major story spoilers in video titles or thumbnails, where they could easily be seen by people who have not yet played the game.<\/strong><\/i><\/u><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Thank you for your understanding and cooperation.<br><br><br><br>All graphics in this game were created by human artists. No generative AI was used.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >We also have a YouTube channel where we upload introduction videos for our layered Clip Studio Paint files, as well as detailed videos showing the work process.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >YouTube: @SUPERTHUMbGameArt<\/p>","short_description":"&quot;Your job is to write the death certificate.&quot; Investigate a mysterious death in a British manor in 1959. Explore eerie scenes, analyze evidence, and complete death certificates and emergency reports. A forensic mystery with art inspired by 1960s European detective comics.","supported_languages":"English, Japanese, Simplified Chinese, Traditional Chinese, Korean","header_image":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/3758950\/30b155b0452ba4b8d69fd2ba081a7237bca92606\/header.jpg?t=1793692815","capsule_image":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/3758950\/83494523e0439365557640726dc4e5f8aa56fa0e\/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1793692815","capsule_imagev5":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/3758950\/83494523e0439365557640726dc4e5f8aa56fa0e\/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1793692815","website":"https:\/\/www.superthumb.net\/flemingm